r matches via majority or both joint majorities; a matching current-term quorum endpoint advances commitment. Append/heartbeat propagate commitment, and Ready dispatches bounded committed prefixes to caller application. Heartbeat responses also restore replication flow after losses; compaction can require snapshot catch-up.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-replication\",\n        \"B-storage\",\n        \"B-config\",\n        \"B-application\",\n        \"B-client\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-commit\",\n        \"F-config\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"s-propose\",\n        \"s-ack\",\n        \"s-replicate\",\n        \"s-logappend\",\n        \"s-logmatch\",\n        \"s-tracker\",\n        \"s-joint\",\n        \"s-majority\",\n        \"s-recovery\",\n        \"s-apply-reset\",\n        \"src-storage-contract\",\n        \"src-ready-storage\",\n        \"src-append-response\",\n        \"src-step-context\",\n        \"src-unstable-retirement\",\n        \"src-stableto\",\n        \"s-send\",\n        \"s-raw-ready\",\n        \"s-ready-contract\",\n        \"s-config\",\n        \"s-changer\",\n        \"s-node-contract\",\n        \"s-applyable\",\n        \"s-logcommit\",\n        \"s-node-loop\",\n        \"s-doc\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"context\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Eligible followers campaign after logical timeout or explicit request, with unapplied committed configuration and pending-snapshot guards. Vote freshness and term/vote rules constrain support; persisted self and remote votes feed current voter quorums. Pre-vote probes without term change. Winning installs leader state and an empty current-term entry. Higher terms, same-term leader traffic to candidates and optional quorum loss change role; reset clears progress, vote tally, read quorum state and transfer while preserving log decisions. Transfer catches up a voter then requests election; proposals pause and timeout aborts transfer. Lower-term network work is rejected or answered with current term; old storage acknowledgments have separate entry/snapshot handling.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-election\",\n        \"B-storage\",\n        \"B-recovery\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-commit\",\n        \"F-config\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"s-authority\",\n        \"src-step-context\",\n        \"s-roles\",\n        \"s-logmatch\",\n        \"s-joint\",\n        \"s-majority\",\n        \"src-storage-contract\",\n        \"src-ready-storage\",\n        \"src-append-response\",\n        \"src-unstable-retirement\",\n        \"src-stableto\",\n        \"s-send\",\n        \"s-raw-ready\",\n        \"s-ready-contract\",\n        \"s-init\",\n        \"s-logappend\",\n        \"s-recovery\",\n        \"s-storage\",\n        \"s-bootstrap\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"connection\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Authority selects whose support can form decisions, but committed history survives authority changes. Log freshness carries prior decisions into elections; current-term commitment qualifies deferred read processing. Configuration application changes both quorum aggregation and election eligibility, and can itself advance commitment using retained matches. Recovery reinstalls history and eligibility. Storage responses are term-filtered for overwrite-sensitive entries, whereas committed snapshot/application progress survives term transitions. Read quorum contexts reset on role change; the separate pre-first-commit request queue requires further lifecycle investigation.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-election\",\n        \"B-replication\",\n        \"B-config\",\n        \"B-read\",\n        \"B-storage\",\n        \"B-recovery\",\n        \"B-application\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-commit\",\n        \"F-config\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"s-authority\",\n        \"src-step-context\",\n        \"s-roles\",\n      