ailability after intended removal. This is a scoped continuation question, not a demonstrated safety failure or a numeric deadline claim.','source_ids':['s-implicit-contract','s-enterjoint','s-autoleave-owner','s-apply-reset','s-authority','s-propose','s-abort-transfer','s-advance','s-transfer-api','s-autoleave-test','s-config'],'participants':['Current leader','Transfer target voter','Other old/new quorum voters','Ready consumer'],'objects':['F-config','Implicit configuration entry','Automatic empty exit proposal','leadTransferee','Applied index'],'contexts':['Synchronous RawNode API with persistence and ordered configuration application before Advance','Implicit joint membership change retaining current leader and transfer target','Finite loss of TimeoutNow followed by fully delivered heartbeats and responses, no new client proposals'],'event_paths':['Commit implicit joint entry -> ApplyConfChange -> TransferLeader before acknowledging application -> Advance invokes appliedTo and exit proposal may be dropped -> ticks expire transfer -> drain Ready and network work','Control: same configuration with no overlapping transfer; rescue: later ordinary entry if the quiescent suffix leaves joint state unchanged'],'activity_classes':['A4','A5','A2','A1'],'behavior_ids':['B-config','B-application'],'fact_ids':['F-config'],'supporting_behavior_ids':{'B-election':'Transfer admission and timeout determine when local proposal suppression ends; role transition is a potential alternate exit trigger.','B-replication':'The configuration entry and a potential exit must obtain actual quorum support; no precommitted synthetic entry will stand in for this history.','B-storage':'Ready/Advance supplies application-completion events only when a committed batch was dispatched.','B-client':'Defines caller ordering, proposal retry limits and externally supplied ticks.'},'obligation_relation_kind':'consumption','counterevidence':['appliedTo retries on each later applied entry; a successful leadership change creates a new leader entry and can restore continuation.','Existing TestRawNodeJointAutoLeave expects automatic exit after losing and regaining leadership, but does not cover transfer timeout under stable leadership; its final direct ApplyConfChange explicitly bypasses joint commitment and cannot be reused as a legal cluster prefix.','Generic client proposals may be dropped and retried by the caller; implicit joint exit has a separate interface-owned automatic transition contract.','No tick deadline is specified for configuration completion.'],'unknowns':['Can a public-API multi-node schedule place transfer between configuration application and its Advance acknowledgment while keeping the actual configuration entry committed and caller ordering legal?','After timeout and full queue drainage, can heartbeat, acknowledgment, Ready, snapshot or application work produce another appliedTo call without unrelated proposals?','Does the observed suffix close all state and scheduling triggers, or only show bounded non-completion?'],'disposition':'concrete_suspicion','preferred_check':'controlled_schedule','priority':2,'trigger_rationale':'appliedTo alone initiates automatic exit, and explicitly permits Step to reject it during transfer. abortLeaderTransfer only clears leadTransferee. Advance generates application responses only for nonempty committed batches. This difference warrants a small real-cluster schedule rather than repeating an isolated guard test.'}}\njson.dump(p,open('submission.json','w'),indent=2)\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));import subprocess;x=subprocess.run(r['validation']['command']+['submission.json'],capture_output=True,text=True);print(x.stdout,x.stderr)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
